Subject: [PATCH 06850/11362] ARC round-3 (codex): m0r0 FULL CLEAR, L5 -> L6
 (+1)

Continuation of round-3. m0r0's previously-unexplained color-9 object
(explored but not won in round 2) turned out to be a movable plug at the
only safe opening in the lethal central checkerboard seam, and a
reusable directional pin -- used three different ways in one solve to
hold pressure plates open while the two players route through gates and
across the seam.

The source agent honestly flagged the win as reproduction_verified=false:
a compressed 297-action gate attempt returned reached_level=0, and with
no budget left to disambiguate a genuine reset from the harness's 0
report on an empty terminal-win frame (both look identical), the
artifact correctly kept the full 401-action live-observed trajectory
rather than the failed compression. Independently re-verified by the
outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay of the FULL sequence via the
fixed resolver, all 5 confirmed reached_level=6 AND state=GameState.WIN.
m0r0 is a confirmed full clear.

reproducible_total_levels: 142 -> 143 (verified against a fresh sum).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
